<!--Render Target Documentation — NativeMappings
  FQN: com.machineblocks.bml.target.render.documentation.NativeMappings-->
<rdoc:NativeMappings xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:rdoc="com.machineblocks.bml.target.render.documentation">

  <baseType>
    core:Documentation
  </baseType>
  <is>
    Declarative map from built-in capabilities to native SCAD functions
  </is>
  <documentation>
    ScadBlockProcessor reads a declarative JSON file, scad-native-mappings.json,
    shipped with this package. It maps #built-in capability calls to native SCAD
    functions when a 1:1 equivalent exists, so trivial calls do not import a
    helper.

    Location: package root of @machineblocks/render-target, file
    scad-native-mappings.json.

    Format: service FQN to function name to { native, arity }.
    native null means no direct SCAD equivalent: emit the FQN-prefixed function
    and add a use import. arity -1 means variadic.

    Initial map:

        org.blockml.bml.service.Math
          min max floor ceil round abs pow sqrt — native of the same name, arity 1 or 2
          round_n clamp — native null
        org.blockml.bml.service.Strings
          length — native len, arity 1
          concat — native str, arity -1

    Resolution for each #built-in in ${ } expressions or in embedded expressions
    inside SCAD implementations:

        #math.min(a, b)       -> min(a, b), no import
        #math.round_n(x, 1)   -> bom__org__blockml__service__Math__round_n(x, 1)
                                 plus use of Math.scad
        #strings.length(s)    -> len(s), no import

    Functions inside the service SCAD files use the bom__ prefix and __ separators:

        function bom__org__blockml__service__Math__round_n(x, n) =
          round(x * pow(10, n)) / pow(10, n);
        function bom__org__blockml__service__Math__clamp(x, lo, hi) =
          min(max(x, lo), hi);

    The same prefix pattern applies to the other Math helpers (min, max, floor,
    ceil, round, abs, pow, sqrt) even when the native map also emits the short
    SCAD name. The service file remains the fallback implementation.

  </documentation>
  <references>
    <see type="rdoc:FileStructure" relation="ReadNext" />
  </references>
</rdoc:NativeMappings>
